      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:36 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I'd like to begin with the statutory text. Section 415(a)(7)(A) is found at petition appendix page 69a, and it excludes from the windfall elimination provision \"a payment based wholly on service as a member of a uniformed service as defined in section 410(m).\" David Babcock, who served as a dual-status technician in the National Guard for 33 years, qualifies. Indeed, 32 U.S.C. 709 requires technicians like him to literally \"wear the uniform of the armed services, be a member of the National Guard, and hold the military grade specified by the Secretary.\" And Babcock did. He wore the U.S. Army uniform day in, day out, teaching people"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Katyal -- MR. KATYAL: -- us civilians don't -- JUSTICE BARRETT: -- what if a private employer said, I'm very patriotic, I really like employing members of the National Guard and all of these same requirements that you're articulating, said I want you to wear your uniform to work, I want you to maintain a certain rank, I want you to maintain a certain fitness level, but Mr. Babcock is doing the same job that he's doing, you know, teaching pilot flight school, but he's doing it for a private employer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How about if they're delivering food to the National Guard? It's a private company with all of the prerequisites that Justice Barrett said and they're delivering mess -- food."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that that's right? Is\nthere a difference? If I say a payment based\nwholly on military service, is that the same as\nor different than this statutory language?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. REAVES",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 1916, Congress authorized states to hire military caretakers, who were the predecessors of dual-status technicians, and states developed a practice where most of these individuals had to be members of the National Guard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have just a minor question. The -- how -- how -- how big a problem is this now that CSRS no longer exists?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So we agree this only impacts folks who are still receiving CSRS benefits that they would have been eligible for before 1984?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Neal K. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, Section 415 looks to service, not status, and, in particular, uniformed status -- service."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6db7207bf8d892f64feb75adff94a43b2a19512e02e932b6e1bd3d572b400be1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6db7207bf8d8-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
